## Why This Question Is Asked
Tests understanding of multi-tenant fairness, backpressure mechanisms, and ordering guarantees in bounded queue systems.

## Key Concepts
- **Per-tenant FIFO ordering**: Each tenant's events are processed in strict arrival order
- **Bounded queues and backpressure**: Upstream producers are throttled when system capacity is reached
- **Tenant-aware drop policy**: Balancing retention across tenants with different traffic profiles
- **Starvation avoidance**: Ensuring no tenant is indefinitely blocked by others

## Code Example
```javascript
class TenantBuffer {
  constructor(maxSize) {
    this.queue = [];
    this.maxSize = maxSize;
  }

  enqueue(event) {
    if (this.queue.length >= this.maxSize) {
      this.queue.shift();
    }
    this.queue.push(event);
  }

  dequeue() {
    return this.queue.shift();
  }

  isEmpty() {
    return this.queue.length === 0;
  }
}

class ConcurrencyController {
  constructor(workerCount, buffers) {
    this.workers = new Array(workerCount).fill(null);
    this.buffers = buffers;
  }

  async processEvent(tenantId, event) {
    const buffer = this.buffers.get(tenantId);
    buffer.enqueue(event);
    return this.dispatchToWorker(tenantId);
  }

  async dispatchToWorker(tenantId) {
    const buffer = this.buffers.get(tenantId);
    if (buffer.isEmpty()) return;
    const event = buffer.dequeue();
    return this.processWithWorker(event);
  }

  async processWithWorker(event) {
    console.log(`Processing event for tenant ${event.tenantId}`);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design correct, robust concurrency under backpressure with priority aging and graceful shutdown.

## Key Concepts
- Bounded queues and backpressure
- Priority-aware scheduling
- Fairness via aging
- Graceful shutdown and cancellation

## Code Example
```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;

class WorkItem { final int priority; final Runnable task; WorkItem(int p, Runnable t){priority=p;this.task=t;} void run(){task.run();} }

public class MultiPriorityScheduler {
  private final BlockingQueue<WorkItem>[] queues = new BlockingQueue[3];
  private volatile boolean running = true;

  @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
  public MultiPriorityScheduler(int cap){
    for(int i=0;i<3;i++) queues[i] = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(cap);
  }

  public boolean submit(WorkItem w, long timeout, TimeUnit unit) throws InterruptedException {
    return queues[w.priority].offer(w, timeout, unit);
  }

  public void start(int workerCount){
    for(int i=0;i<workerCount;i++){
      new Thread(() -> {
        while(running){
          WorkItem w=null;
          for(int p=0;p<3;p++){
            w = queues[p].poll(50, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
            if (w != null){ w.run(); break; }
          }
        }
      }).start();
    }
  }

  public void stop(){ running = false; }
}
```

